#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Phase 444: CLAUDE.md -- the log row.
import sys, re
p = sys.argv[1]; s = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()
ROW = """| 444 | 2026-10-12 | **The black key is a hidden attic; no '--' anywhere a reader looks.** Her 16:04 '검은건반을 숨겨진 다락방처럼 내가 쓸 떄도 있고 d가 쓸때도 있고 이렇게 말하는것도 나쁘지 않겠다'; 16:07 '-- 이거 없애주고', then (asked: a real dash, or rewrite) 'rewrite without dashes'; 16:17 '이거 하고 다음순서'. (1) Chapter 11 page 5: 'A black key is like a hidden attic between two rooms, shared by the neighbours on each side. When Clara uses it from C, it is C sharp. When the Dog uses it from D, it is D flat. One attic, two names. But between E and F there is no attic ... so E sharp is the same key as F. A sharp or a flat is not always a black key.' (숨겨진 다락방; 다락방 하나, 이름 둘); the try-it 'The same black key, the same attic!'; the moving part: 'C♯: a half step up from C, into the attic on its right. The neighbour on the other side calls it D♭.' and 'E♯: no attic between E and F, so a half step up from E is the white key F next door. The same key! A sharp is not always a black key.'; Teacher copy say: 'A black key is a hidden attic two neighbours share ...'. (2) Every reader-visible ' -- ' in the app, the books, the Workbooks, the Teacher copies and the toolbox rewritten with a colon, a comma, a full stop or parentheses (2,008 strings; 12 parallel rewriters on one rule sheet, _workspace/chapter-review/g444/x/dash/RULES.md, items.json + out_NN.json; applied by position, dashapply.js); identical strings rewritten identically (lookup keys such as PAT_ROW_KO and MELODY_WHY_KO still match); code that cut text at ' --' now cuts at ':' (the time-signature quiz labels); the print-curation regexes follow the new text; the empty-value placeholders '--' are a single '–'; two Korean typos '생대 G' -> '여왕 G'. Left: the dash glue in the line-break observer (harmless), comments in code. Guide pages (they use em dashes) not touched yet. Checks: a sweep of 96 pages (every chapter, every book, en/ko) finds no '--'; lbcheck chapters 1, 2, 4, 6, 7, 11, 15 no overflow; wbcheck those chapters pass; ch1app376 21, ch2app395 21, ch3app397 35, sf405 22, ll431 24, ll444 82 (from ll429, punctuation-tolerant), ws419 45, nosong399 24, tn444 16 (attic messages; no ' --' in the book), house443 63. |
"""
m = re.search(r'^\| 443 \| [^\n]*\n', s, re.M)
if not m: raise SystemExit('row 443')
s = s[:m.end()] + ROW + s[m.end():]
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s); print('CLAUDE.md: log row 444')
